  "description": "<div>\n<p>Count the bits set to 1 in the 32-bit unsigned binary representation of n. Leading zero bits count as part of the width but do not add to the total.</p>\n<p><strong>Example 1:</strong></p>\n<pre><strong>Input:</strong> n = 11\n<strong>Output:</strong> 3\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> The low bits of 11 are 1011, which contains three ones.</pre>\n<p><strong>Example 2:</strong></p>\n<pre><strong>Input:</strong> n = 128\n<strong>Output:</strong> 1\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> A power of two has exactly one set bit.</pre>\n<p><strong>Example 3:</strong></p>\n<pre><strong>Input:</strong> n = 0\n<strong>Output:</strong> 0\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> All 32 bits of zero are clear.</pre>\n<p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>0 &lt;= n &lt;= 4,294,967,295</code> (an unsigned 32-bit integer).</li>\n<li>The answer is between 0 and 32 inclusive.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>",
